WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
In the next verse of the Shevua, he says something very strange that nobody really knows, I don't

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.000
know of any Mephiles, he says that Moshe Rabbeinu, that all the people that were afraid, Moshe

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Rabbeinu, we don't really know what that means exactly, but somehow it has to do with life.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:48.000
And they were afraid, Moshe Rabbeinu called them, and after he speaks to them, he put

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
masveh al panah, he covered his face, then the people let go, and then the Torah says,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.000
and every time that he would go to speak to the Teshachor, he would remove the masveh

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.000
al panah, he would speak to G-d, and when he goes to speak to the Jewish people, he

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
removes his masveh, no he removes the masveh.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Now, so therefore, I disagree, when he is alone, at home, he covers his face, nobody

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:35.000
sees him, he covers his face, when he is speaking to Borei Olam, or when he is speaking to Am

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:49.000
then he removes his masveh. A few comments, one of the great hachamim coming out from

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Zepharath, or really from Portugal in 1492, now a little bit after 1492, was Rabbi Yosef

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Ya'aves, was a great great hachamim, and when he left Portugal eventually he goes to

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Thessaloniki, and he establishes a printing press, he writes dozens and dozens of books,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:18.000
and of course he prints books, and you know, like, and was such a pious and righteous man

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:28.000
that he is called Rabbi Yosef HaHasid, because he was really a true pious man, and terribly

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.000
intelligent, terribly, terribly intelligent, I mean, unusual, even among intelligent people

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.000
he was unusually intelligent. So, you know there is always, we speak about Allah and

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Baba, and the people say, you were there, huh? So he says, yes, one of the hachamim

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:09.000
was Rabbi Yosef HaHasid. What about Baba? Is, and I use my own word, palingenesis. Palingenesis

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:16.000
means a second birth. I explain exactly, exactly what it means. The word was used, it's a Greek

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.000
word, but it came to English language, that's why I'm using it. And the first people who

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:27.000
used it in a certain manner was, they were Jews, Yosefus and Philo. What it says? It

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:39.000
says, we are born. And then, there is another birth. Palingenesis means a second birth.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Allah and Baba is a second birth. In a sense, Moshe Rabbeinu, when he went to Shammai, his

00:03:49.000 --> 00:04:01.000
whole metabolism, his body changed. The reason that he didn't have to eat is because there

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:08.000
was a biological change, a metabolic change. And as Rabbi Yosef HaHasid says, at the end

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.000
of his life, look how I die now. And I say, how? And not because he was Superman, who

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.000
was stronger than me, or you, but because it was a different evolution, a different

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:33.000
step in human evolution. So, in a sense, Moshe Rabbeinu represents, I like to use English

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:41.000
words because we are an English speaking society, Omega Man, the man of the future. If I have

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:48.000
to conceive Tehiyat HaMetim, I conceive Tehiyat HaMetim. I may be wrong. If I have to conceive

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.000
in my own words, what is Tehiyat HaMetim, Tehiyat HaMetim people would be like Moshe

00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Rabbeinu. Look how I die now, and I say, how? We are going to be, Palingenesis, born and

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:14.000
birth again. And therefore Moshe Rabbeinu was able to travel between this world and

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:25.000
the next world. It was simple. He could travel. For us it seems impossible because our intelligence

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:31.000
has not developed. I am a believer in condition of hope because if I would tell 500 years

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:37.000
ago, somebody had to fly to the moon and so on, they cannot understand. Not because the

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:44.000
words choose me, because they didn't develop to that. And in a sense, Moshe Rabbeinu is

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:59.000
the final goal. The final goal means more than this. It is a step beyond the final goal.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:08.000
Yes, but he is already in a different stage. He is Lokat HaAinov. HaRambam makes a very

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:18.000
nice point about Moshe Rabbeinu. He did not see Borea Olam because he fasted, but he fasted

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:27.000
because he saw Borea Olam. By seeing Borea Olam, by being in the presence of Borea Olam,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:34.000
your biology changes. You don't have to go with a shot. Not because you have to make an effort

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:43.000
to restrain his biological impulse, but because once you see Borea Olam, you have a different

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:51.000
bandrega. You change. And because you change, you don't want to eat. You are not interested

00:06:51.000 --> 00:07:00.000
in eating. The first thing that Moshe Rabbeinu did when he came down from Hassinai was not

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:17.000
to drink, to have a glass of orange juice. He was not hungry. That's important.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:32.000
So, when he was in the presence of Borea Olam, his body changed. Karan or Panav. He was translucent.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Somehow, something is odd. He was there and he was not there. He was translucent. He changed.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:08:00.000
Translucent. Karan or Panav. Now, I explained a little bit. I want to continue explaining,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:14.000
but before I digress, dig on him. In Halamban, beginning with Zed Agaon and all the way up

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:23.000
in Halamban. Moshe Rabbeinu is in Madrigal by himself. He is not like a regular Nabi.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:33.000
The Lokambe style Nabi ki Moshe Rabbeinu. There is no body like that.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Dig on him. In Halamban, we use an Arabic word to designate Moshe Rabbeinu. Shaliyah, Rasul.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:09:00.000
He is the Shalmi of Halamban. Let's be a little bit more explicit or more detailed.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:10.000
When Borea Olam appears in Hashimayim, we hear God telling Moshe Rabbeinu,

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Dabbel bin Israeel. Inay, aniva eleka ba'ar he'anan, ba'ur yishma ha'am beidabbeli itan.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:32.000
Begam becha, ya Amirul Ra'olam. They got to hear me, Borea Olam says, speaking to you.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:41.000
And he got to believe in you. As Halamban explains, he got to believe that I am the Shaliyah, Amitatish, the Shaliyah of Borea Olam.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:50.000
So good. That's one. Any of the mizvot or the geonim in Halamban.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:10:03.000
The mizvot has to come directly from Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:11.000
How? Because the geonim in Halamban, they believe that the mizvot to listen to the Chachamim is Mitzvah Menah Torah.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:22.000
So therefore, if I make a Tilat Yadayim, I read the Halam, I make a Mitzvah Menah Torah.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:29.000
And therefore I could say in the Halem Tzayim Chanukah, Asher Gideshano B'Nusrata, to listen to the Chachamim.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:37.000
And that's for L'Azik Mea Chanukah, or L'Azik Adit Yadayim, or whatever is in Halam.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:48.000
So therefore, Alulam, all this, Alulam, for instance, Bitzman Hazem, during the six days, after the first day, is no longer the Menah Torah.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.000
But I could say, Asher Gideshano B'Nusrata, no, I need that Torah, because I am listening to the Chachamim.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:59.000
And why do I listen to the Chachamim? Because they are great? No, because that told me to listen to the Chachamim.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.000
It's none of our business. B'nei Yonam told me to listen to the Chachamim.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Al piah torah shehagid olecha, lo tashur minadabra shehagid olecha. No, no, no. That's it. I listen to the Chachamim.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Chachamim Va, Elton, Superman, I don't care. That's secondary thing. B'nei Yonam told me.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:25.000
So therefore, Mizvah, for the Rambam, for the Yoni, has to provide, come, only for Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Yeshayah, Yirmeyach, the greatest prophet.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:40.000
Their role is not to tell me a new Mizvah, but to tell me to obey the Mizvah of the Avorei Olam, gate to Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:46.000
No prophet could be Mechadesh Torah. What the prophet could do?

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:57.000
Rebuke you, why aren't you, or aren't we, fulfilling the Mizvah of the Avorei Olam, to Moshe Rabbeinu?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:06.000
So therefore, Moshe Rabbeinu is in the Madrigal by himself.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.000
Now to understand what the Pirashah says, not to speak.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.000
I have another question.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:19.000
Let me tell you how I picture Yirmeyach, or Yeshayah, or Amos, or Sheyach.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:34.000
I picture somehow where Olam comes in a dream, or in Mahazein, it tells Yahezkel, or Amos, say X.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:48.000
After the Mahazein, or the Hezion, or whatever it is, he is awake, comes back into God, and he goes to deliver the message.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:52.000
He is not a Shaliyah.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.000
When Moshe does that, he is a Shaliyah. What is the difference?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Let me tell you my opinion, it's only an opinion, and I have some proofs, but I don't see it written in any place except the Torah.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:08.000
And I think it's a very nice point.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.000
When Yeshayah delivers the message, he is no longer in a prophetic trance.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:19.000
He had a prophecy X time ago, an hour ago, 10 hours ago, a day ago.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.000
Now he comes to deliver the message.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:27.000
When he delivers the message, he is talking into your ear, language.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.000
He is Yeshayah, the human being.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:40.000
Potentially, of course, yesterday it was Nabi, but right now, he is a foreign Nabi in a sense.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:49.000
I mean, he heard it, of course he heard it, but as he delivers, he is not a Nabi.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:54.000
He comes to understand what the Torah is saying.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:14:01.000
When Moshe Rabbeinu spoke to Borei Olam, they must leave.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:05.000
It is the work of a scheme.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:11.000
I don't know what level of the scheme, I mean, I am not a scheme doctor, I don't know what level of the scheme.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.000
They disappeared.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:20.000
The whole thing disappeared.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:24.000
Borei Olam is speaking to him.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Also, when he was speaking to Bnei Yisrael, also Karan opened up.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:38.000
They must say he puts it only when he is not speaking to Borei Olam or he is not speaking with Bnei Yisrael.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:46.000
The three weeks for him speaking to Borei Olam and speaking to Bnei Yisrael,

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.000
they were two sides of the same picture.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:56.000
Simultaneously, as Borei Olam speaks to him, he is speaking to us.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.000
We are the witnesses.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:05.000
We see, so to speak, Moshe Rabbeinu speaking to God.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:13.000
He is the shaniach because as he speaks to us, Karan opened up.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:20.000
And here that is a thing, I have a re'ayah for it, I am going to tell you in a second.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.000
Yes?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:30.000
That when the whole idea of the Mishkan, how Moshe Rabbeinu delivered the Torah to Am Yisrael,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:37.000
it is not that he was a Nabi, at 5 o'clock in the morning, comes at 11 o'clock, whatever the time,

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:40.000
I have an important message to give you.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.000
And he delivers to you and his parim is regular parim like yours and mine.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.000
No, that was not the case.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:54.000
He is a shaniach because he is at the same time, the words of Borei Olam are reflected,

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.000
Karan I think is reflected.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:05.000
Not transparent, I said translucent at the beginning, but I don't think he is translucent.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.000
I think he is projecting.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
He is projecting.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.000
Yes?

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Alright?

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.000
And he projects the thing.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:28.000
In a separate terashah, and a great hakan, Rabbi Moshe Adsheikh,

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:34.000
if you want, I hope that all of you will have the proficiency in Hebrew and Jewish knowledge

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.000
to read the terashot of Rabbi Moshe Adsheikh.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.000
He was Tamit of Marana Kalosh, that's not a joke.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.000
He was Dayan in Safed, that's not a joke.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.000
And his terashot are, yes, they show him to Jewah, because he was a Dayan.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.000
But his terashot are massive.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.000
He was an artist.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.000
He was an artist of the terashah.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:57.000
And what I like of this terashanim, like Rabbi Moshe Adsheikh,

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:02.000
I mean, the truth is that the terashah is Peshat.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.000
He has a question.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.000
It doesn't relate to the terashah.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
I'm relating it to the terashah.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.000
He has another question and he says,

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:15.000
and then when Rabbi Moshe Adsheikh was telling me to Aharon and to Miriam,

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:19.000
the difference between all other Nebihim and Moshe Rabbeinu,

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.000
he says, look in Moshe Abdi.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.000
There is a difference.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.000
And one of the Nebihim says,

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.000
P and P, Adaber Bo.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:36.000
And the other Nebihim is wrong.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:41.000
The person who says P and P, Adaber Lo.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:48.000
What does it mean, P and P, Adaber Bo?

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.000
Rabbi Moshe Adsheikh says,

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:58.000
השכינה הייתה מדברת מתוך גרונו של Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.000
P and P, Adaber Bo.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:07.000
Like the mouth of B'Olam would be inside the mouth of Moshe Rabbeinu.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:13.000
And I think this is what the terashah,

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
next week the terashah is telling us.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.000
How P and P, Adaber Bo.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:23.000
We saw Moshe Rabbeinu talking to God.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:27.000
When he says, وَيُدَبَّرْ أَدُونَيِّ الْمُشَيْنِ لِمَوْرٍ

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.000
That was simultaneous.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:34.000
Not like, وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ لِمَوْرٍ

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:40.000
وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ الْمُشَيْنِ لِمَوْرٍ is a single sentence.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:46.000
Both, speaking to God and speaking to Israel,

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.000
occur simultaneously, at the same time.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:55.000
When he was not talking to B'Olam, he was not talking to Israel.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:59.000
The masfeh fell down automatically in his face.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:04.000
And when he spoke to B'Olam, he spoke to Israel.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:08.000
So what would be the difference in, وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:12.000
No, always, وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ لِمَوْرٍ

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:18.000
Ah, there should be a difference. I don't know the difference.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:22.000
But I know that if the Torah says, وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.000
There must be a difference. I don't know the difference.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.000
I mean, yes, I'm sure that there is a difference.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:33.000
There cannot be, that is a hazard, that is fortuitous.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
But there are things I don't know.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:40.000
Now, as a teacher, I think I do good.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:43.000
If I know, I say, I don't know.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.000
If I don't know, the worst thing I could say is,

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.000
وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.000
Why? No, no, I'll tell you why.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.000
Because if I give a big proof, or something like this,

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.000
then I may convince you that you have an answer,

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:00.000
and you're not going to think about it.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:07.000
If I say, I don't know, maybe one day, I will not have an answer.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:09.000
Or you tell the question to another person,

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.000
and the other person will have an answer.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:15.000
So, yes, I believe that there is a difference between

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.000
وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ and وَيُدَبَّرْ هَشَمْ أَحْنَحْ الْمُشَيْنِ

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.000
What's the difference?

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:26.000
So now, here, we have something which is central about Judaism.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:31.000
In a sense, we are not Omega Man.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:35.000
We're not Superman.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:40.000
But we were in contact with Superman.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
With Omega Man.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:48.000
We know that there is Olam Abba.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:51.000
Although we were not there, we saw.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:57.000
During the 40 years of transmitting the triumph in the desert,

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:02.000
we saw, we witnessed Olam Abba.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.000
We witnessed a man, our teacher.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:10.000
We graduate, we have Semicha, every Yehudi has Semicha.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.000
From Moshe, Rabbeinu.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.000
We saw the man.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Our mom says something which is hard to say nowadays,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.000
but he says it.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:27.000
And I write it, I try to write it in a polite way and so on.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.000
We don't want to offend Hashem Shalom.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.000
But our mom says that all this experience,

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.000
she doesn't use the word, but if I have to tell you in English,

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.000
it's a phylogenetic experience.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:46.000
It becomes a shape of personality.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:52.000
And it's transmitted from children to parents.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.000
I'm sorry, from parents to children, from generation to generation.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.000
Genetically.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.000
What?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Genetically.

